---
import InfoLayout from '../layouts/InfoLayout.astro';
import { SITE_CONFIG } from '../config/site';
import { TOOLS } from '../config/tools';

const name = SITE_CONFIG.name;
const adsEnabled = Boolean(import.meta.env.PUBLIC_ADSENSE_CLIENT);
---

<InfoLayout
  title="About"
  description={`${name} is a free set of ${TOOLS.length} image tools that run in your browser, in 10 languages, with no uploads and no sign-up.`}
  path="about"
>
  <p>
    {name} is a free set of {TOOLS.length} image tools (crop, resize, compress, convert, remove backgrounds, make PDFs and more) that
    work entirely in your web browser. It is available in 10 languages and needs no account.
  </p>

  <h2>Why it exists</h2>
  <p>
    Most online image tools upload your photo to a server to edit it. That is slow on a weak connection, and it means handing your
    personal photos, documents and ID pictures to someone else. Modern browsers are powerful enough to do this work themselves, so
    here every tool runs on your own device. Your images never leave it.
  </p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>In your browser:</strong> image editing uses the browser's canvas and WebAssembly, the same technology that runs games and video editors on the web.</li>
    <li><strong>AI on your device:</strong> the background remover downloads a model once and runs it locally. Your photo is never sent anywhere.</li>
    <li><strong>Works offline:</strong> after your first visit, the tools keep working without an internet connection.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Built for everyone</h2>
  <p>
    Every tool works on a phone and can be used with a keyboard alone, with a screen reader, at large zoom levels and in high-contrast
    mode. Read the <a href="/accessibility">accessibility statement</a> for details.
  </p>

  <h2>Who makes it</h2>
  <p>
    {name} is built and maintained by {SITE_CONFIG.operator} in {SITE_CONFIG.operatorCountry}. The code is open source under the
    AGPL-3.0 license: you can <a href={SITE_CONFIG.sourceUrl} rel="noopener">read it, check what it does, and suggest changes</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Keeping it free</h2>
  <p>
    {adsEnabled
      ? 'The tools are free. Ads between page sections help pay for hosting; they never receive your images. See the privacy policy for details.'
      : 'The tools are free to use, with no sign-up and no watermarks.'}
  </p>

  <h2>Get in touch</h2>
  <p>
    Found a bug or want a tool that isn't here? <a href="/contact">Contact us</a>.
  </p>
</InfoLayout>
